<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kralice Bible</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1579">1579</a>–<a href="/years/1593">1593</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Bible of Kralice</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kralice Bible is the first complete Czech translation of the Bible from the original <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew">Hebrew</a> and Greek, made by scholars of the Unity of the Brethren and printed at Kralice nad Oslavou in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a> in six volumes between 1579 and 1593. Its language became the model for literary Czech, and it remained the standard Protestant Czech Bible for centuries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kralice-bible.jpg" alt="Kralice Bible" width="265" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kralice.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
